  "body": "The [Welcome and Overview page](https://matrix-org.github.io/synapse/develop/welcome_and_overview.html) is the first page that people see when they visit Synapse's documentation website. At the moment it's fairly bare. We received some feedback from the community on the content one might expect to see there, and I largely agree.\r\n\r\nFrom Nicolas Guichard in [#synapse:matrix.org](https://matrix.to/#/#synapse:matrix.org), it would be nice to see:\r\n\r\n* something that explains a bit more what Synapse is and what it's not, to know if I should continue reading or not\r\n* big buttons to the most important sections of the documentation (install, configure, admin, contribute)\r\n* and/or something like the following to fill up the Space™?\r\n\r\n![Matrix software map](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/1342360/120791116-af491500-c52b-11eb-8045-389b2ef4b1a4.jpeg)\r\n",
